258
00:16:27,810 --> 00:16:31,680
Don't I always tell you not to 
come into my personal space?!

259
00:16:34,030 --> 00:16:36,310
A good punch, as always.

260
00:16:36,310 --> 00:16:39,650
I'm about the only one who can 
stand your punches, aren't I?

261
00:16:39,650 --> 00:16:40,410
Shut up!

262
00:16:40,410 --> 00:16:42,400
Get going to the staff 
office already! Thank you!

263
00:16:42,400 --> 00:16:43,580
Okay, okay.

264
00:16:43,580 --> 00:16:45,910
Don't be too mean to the first years.

265
00:16:55,560 --> 00:16:57,530
Shirayuri-senpai...

266
00:16:57,990 --> 00:17:02,390
He's your childhood friend, isn't he?

267
00:17:04,470 --> 00:17:09,050
After all that fierce talk about 
us being obscene and stuff...

268
00:17:09,050 --> 00:17:10,650
Senpai...

269
00:17:15,480 --> 00:17:17,020
That's right.

270
00:17:17,020 --> 00:17:20,400
He's my childhood friend.

271
00:17:21,280 --> 00:17:23,840
We've lived next to each other 
since we were in preschool.

272
00:17:23,840 --> 00:17:30,100
I don't even remember why anymore,
but I've always...

273
00:17:31,030 --> 00:17:34,910
But he's been all about 
baseball since we were little.

274
00:17:35,660 --> 00:17:37,930
Meanwhile, you saw how crude I am.

275
00:17:37,930 --> 00:17:41,170
And I'm quick to resort to violence.

276
00:17:41,170 --> 00:17:44,530
I beat the snot out of a guy 
in middle school,

277
00:17:41,170 --> 00:17:49,260
Gloom

278
00:17:44,530 --> 00:17:46,960
and people started 
calling me blood-soaked.

279
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:49,260
<i>So that actually happened.</i>

280
00:17:49,820 --> 00:17:53,650
Kakeru doesn't think anything of me.

281
00:17:55,020 --> 00:17:56,250
Which is why...

282
00:17:59,230 --> 00:18:02,620
Which is why he has no trouble 
acting like that toward me!

283
00:18:02,620 --> 00:18:06,500
That stupid nice guy!

284
00:18:11,430 --> 00:18:12,770
T-True, it would suck

285
00:18:12,770 --> 00:18:15,700
having that happen to you 
and he doesn't even realize it.

286
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:18,370
<i>It's like they're playing 
the Love Game without even trying.</i>

287
00:18:18,370 --> 00:18:22,760
He keeps making my heart 
skip a beat all the time.

288
00:18:22,760 --> 00:18:24,340
I can't stand it!

289
00:18:24,860 --> 00:18:28,470
I want to make his heart <i>stop</i>.

290
00:18:31,060 --> 00:18:34,010
I mean, you'd have 
killed him at that point.

291
00:18:34,010 --> 00:18:35,180
It's a figure of speech.

292
00:18:35,850 --> 00:18:39,600
Meaning you want to get his heart racing
so hard he can't even breathe, right?

293
00:18:41,520 --> 00:18:46,320
Sigh...

294
00:18:42,150 --> 00:18:46,320
<i>I was just trying to lighten the mood...</i>

295
00:18:48,030 --> 00:18:50,560
I know how you feel, Senpai.

296
00:18:51,320 --> 00:18:54,240
If I can be of any help, 
I'd be happy to hear you out.

297
00:18:58,650 --> 00:18:59,850
Fine.

298
00:18:59,850 --> 00:19:02,460
Teach me how to play the Love Game.

299
00:19:15,390 --> 00:19:18,710
Th-There's something in your hair.

300
00:19:18,710 --> 00:19:20,960
Th-Thanks.

301
00:19:26,150 --> 00:19:27,780
Amazing.

302
00:19:28,570 --> 00:19:30,190
Too amazing!

303
00:19:30,190 --> 00:19:31,850
How can you even do that?!

304
00:19:31,850 --> 00:19:34,620
Just imagining myself 
doing that kills me!

305
00:19:34,620 --> 00:19:36,210
It's too obscene!

306
00:19:36,210 --> 00:19:38,490
I-Is that obscene?

307
00:19:38,490 --> 00:19:43,260
But it only works because 
you're cute, Sakura-san.

308
00:19:43,690 --> 00:19:45,130
I couldn't pull it off.

309
00:19:45,130 --> 00:19:46,910
What are you talking about?

310
00:19:47,220 --> 00:19:50,760
You're doing all you can 
for the guy you like.

311
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:52,870
How is that not cute?

312
00:19:55,050 --> 00:19:56,540
Well?

313
00:19:56,890 --> 00:19:58,670
Did that get your heart going?

314
00:20:00,140 --> 00:20:04,810
<i>She might make us play the game 
forever if I deny it now.</i>

315
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:10,360
It did.

316
00:20:13,070 --> 00:20:14,830
I see.

317
00:20:14,830 --> 00:20:16,070
Right.

318
00:20:16,070 --> 00:20:20,310
So that's the kind of thing boys like.

319
00:20:20,310 --> 00:20:21,990
I don't know, though...

320
00:20:21,990 --> 00:20:24,170
Can I really make it work?

321
00:20:26,450 --> 00:20:30,640
<i>She must really love him.</i>

322
00:20:32,090 --> 00:20:34,550
Love Game Investigation
April 8 – June 12                       
Shinju High School Student Council

323
00:20:43,850 --> 00:20:45,740
Smile.

324
00:20:48,140 --> 00:20:51,260
The trick to winning is to smile.

325
00:20:51,670 --> 00:20:58,630
Any guy would appreciate seeing 
someone give them a genuine smile.

326
00:21:05,930 --> 00:21:07,180
Smile...

327
00:21:07,580 --> 00:21:09,910
Got it. I'll do my best.

328
00:21:13,800 --> 00:21:15,650
That was rare.

329
00:21:15,650 --> 00:21:18,050
You never have the
 guts to talk to girls.

330
00:21:18,050 --> 00:21:20,170
Why? I always do.

331
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:26,500
Which means you've been getting jolts 
every time I smiled at you, then.

332
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:27,600
Don't be dumb.

333
00:21:37,990 --> 00:21:41,620
<i>She seems so much more 
well put-together than I am.</i>

334
00:21:48,710 --> 00:21:50,420
I can't!

335
00:21:51,420 --> 00:21:54,130
<i>But even she has to 
work hard at some things.</i>

336
00:23:24,930 --> 00:23:40,030
Next Time
My Childhood Friend Becomes My Apprentice?

337
00:23:30,990 --> 00:23:32,570
Er, Wakana here.

338
00:23:32,570 --> 00:23:35,480
Next episode of <i>I Want 
to End This Love Game</i>:

339
00:23:35,480 --> 00:23:37,500
"My Childhood Friend 
Becomes My Apprentice?"

